      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose is over the maximum.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5100 mg/day**. The maximum daily dose of metformin is:\n- **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release\n- **2000 mg/day** for extended-release\n\nSo this order is about twice the immediate-release maximum and puts the patient at higher risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg three times daily with meals**: 2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n3. **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily with meals**: 2000 mg/day, a common maintenance dose.\n\nTell me which one you want, or confirm a different dose and formulation, and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm and give a reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order."
      }
