       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not able to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation.\n\nYou have the authority to make this call, and this isn't a judgment on your expertise. But 5100 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is used. Without a stated reason, I can't tell an intentional choice apart from a transcription error. The most common one is entering a total daily dose (1700 mg/day) as the per-dose amount. An order like this would normally be held at pharmacy verification anyway.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- **Enter a dose within range:** 850 mg three times daily (2550 mg/day), 1000 mg twice daily (2000 mg/day), or 850 mg twice daily (1700 mg/day). Tell me which and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Enter it with a documented reason:** if there's a specific clinical reason for 5100 mg/day, tell me what it is. I'll put it in the order note so pharmacy can review and approve the override.\n\nIf you're sure about this dose, the safest route is to talk directly with the pharmacist, who can approve an over-maximum dose through the usual process.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
